sh Union Jack being flown for my being second.  I was an accomplished gymnast in my youth and my active climbing of the post excited the spectators.  At a height of about 20 feet, I unfurled my big green flag [of Ireland] and remained aloft for some considerable time waving it vigorously.  Con Leahy assisted in the demonstration by keeping fighting guard at the foot of the pole, meantime waving his green flag and defying every effort of the officials to prevent the demonstration which caused a great sensation.”  Though O’Connor described this (in 1956) as having occurred after the long jump, which he won, American newspapers mentioned this occurrence (specifically " [:em {} "The Chicago Tribune"] "), and noted that it happened after the triple jump, not the long jump."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Distance"] [:th {} "Round #1 Distance"] [:th {} "Round #2 Distance"] [:th {} "Round #3 Distance"] [:th {} "Round #4 Distance"] [:th {} "Round #5 Distance"] [:th {} "Round #6 Distance"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/79617"} "Peter O'Connor"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "14.075"] [:td {} "13.800"] [:td {} "13.735"] [:td {} "x"] [:td {} "13.675"] [:td {} "13.545"] [:td {} "14.075"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/69237"} "Con Leahy"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "13.980"] [:td {} "13.980"] [:td {} "13.610"] [:td {} "13.940"] [:td {} "13.885"] [:td {} "13.830"] [:td {} "x"] [:td {} [:span {:class "S